::modern-treasury ns
meta {
    doc: """
    Modern Treasury API bindings: payment operations on top of your own
    bank accounts, plus a double-entry ledger.

    - `::modern-treasury::counterparties` and
      `::modern-treasury::external-accounts`: who you pay, their bank
      accounts, and micro-deposit verification
    - `::modern-treasury::internal-accounts`: your bank accounts and
      their balance reports
    - `::modern-treasury::payment-orders`: send (`credit`) or pull
      (`debit`) money over ACH, wire, RTP, check, book and other rails;
      approve, cancel and reverse
    - `::modern-treasury::expected-payments`: payments you expect to
      receive, for reconciliation
    - `::modern-treasury::transactions`: bank transactions as reported
      by the bank
    - `::modern-treasury::ledgers`: ledgers, ledger accounts, ledger
      transactions, ledger entries and balances
    - `::modern-treasury::returns` and
      `::modern-treasury::incoming-payment-details`
    - `::modern-treasury::events`, `::modern-treasury::webhooks`
      (`X-Signature` verification) and `::modern-treasury::simulations`
      (sandbox only)
    - `::modern-treasury::api`: transport, errors, pagination and the
      `call` escape hatch

    **Setup**: context variables
    - `modern-treasury.organization.id` and `modern-treasury.api.key`
      (Developers → API Keys); they are the Basic auth user and password
    - `modern-treasury.environment`: `"sandbox"` or `"production"`. Both
      use the same host; it only unlocks the sandbox simulations
    - `modern-treasury.webhook.key`: the webhook key from Developers →
      Webhooks

    **Money movement.** Creating a payment order, a reversal or a return
    needs an `idempotency-key` in its trailing `opts` Map and errs locally
    without one. Nothing in this package retries a request. Agents should
    leave approval to a person: configure approval rules in Modern
    Treasury so agent-created orders wait in `needs_approval`.

    **Quick start**

    ```hot
    ::api ::modern-treasury::api
    ::po ::modern-treasury::payment-orders

    accounts ::modern-treasury::internal-accounts/list-internal-accounts({per_page: 10})

    order ::po/create-payment-order({
      type: "ach",
      direction: "credit",
      amount: 10000,
      originating_account_id: "0f8e3719-3dfd-4613-9bbf-c0333781b59f",
      receiving_account_id: "5acec2ef-987b-4260-aa97-b719eeb0a8d5",
      description: "Invoice 42"
    }, {idempotency-key: "invoice-42-payout"})
    ```
    """
}

BASE_URL "https://app.moderntreasury.com"

// The default and maximum `per_page` of Modern Treasury list endpoints.
MAX_PAGE_SIZE 100
